course: dictionary
lesson: 2718
title: Sound words and everyday meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. «Ding» is a good example. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning is right.
explain: A ding can be a sound: a short ringing noise, like a bell or a timer. «The oven timer dings, so the cake is ready.» The words oven and timer are the clues that it is a sound.
explain: A ding can also be a small dent or mark, often on a car. «There is a ding in the car door.» The word door and the idea of a mark are the clues here. To ding can be a verb too: it means to ring, or to dent something slightly.
explain: Ding is also a sound word, because it sounds like the noise it makes. Writers use sound words to help us hear a story.
fact: A ding is a short ringing sound, like a bell or a timer.
fact: In American and Australian English, a ding is a small dent or mark, often on a car.
fact: To ding means to make a ringing sound, or to dent something slightly.
fact: Ding is a sound word, called onomatopoeia, because it sounds like what it means.
fact: In «every ding had been real money», the ding is a sound from a tablet, not a bell.
exercise: «The oven timer dings, so the cake is ready.» What does dings mean here? | *It makes a short ringing sound | It goes very slowly | It makes a small dent in the oven | It is switched off for the night
exercise: «There is a ding in the car door after the car park.» What is the ding? | A bell in the garden | *A small dent or mark | A type of car | A loud song
exercise: Which word in «the phone went ding with a message» copies a sound? | phone | message | *ding | went
test: «Mum's card had been saved on the tablet, so every ding had been real money.» What does ding mean here? | A shout for help | A bell at the church | *A sound from the tablet, meaning money had been taken | A small dent on the tablet
test: Which sentence uses ding as a verb, an action word? | Ding! is a fun word. | The bell went ding. | *The lift will ding when it arrives. | A ding is in the car door.
exam: In «The lift dinged, and there was a ding on the van door», what are the two meanings of ding? | A dent and a dent | A song and a game | Two bells | *A ringing sound, and a small dent
